By using Array Module
----------------------
- An array is a collection of elements of the same datatype stored in
  contiguous memory locations
- To create an array in Python, import the array module and use its array()
  function.

'i' = Integer list
'u' = Character
'd' = decimal

import array as arr
# creating an array with integer type
a = arr.array('i', [1, 2, 3])
print (a)
# creating an array with char type
a = arr.array('u', 'AVD')
print (a)
# creating an array with float type
a = arr.array('d', [1.1, 2.2, 3.3])
print (a)

Eg.
---
import array
arr=array.array('i',[10,20,30])
print(*arr)

or use alias name

import array as arr
arr=arr.array('i',[10,20,30]) #arr=module array=method
print(*arr)

INSERTION
---------
import array
arr=array.array('i',[10,20,30])
arr.append(40)
print(*arr)

-All methods,function as same as list.

Operations
---------
Traverse − Print all the array elements one by one by using index number
Insertion − Adds an element at the given index by using insert( ) method
Deletion − Deletes an element at the given index by using remove( )
Search − Searches an element using the given index or by the value.
Update − Updates an element at the given index.

Ex:
import array as arr
a = arr.array('i',[10, 20, 30, 15])
#To Print all Elements
for i in a:
print(i,end='\t')
#To print all elements by using index number
for i in range(len(a)):
print(a[i],end='\t')
#Add 22 element
a.append(22)
a.insert(2,12)
print(a)
